==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|fr|tarif}}, from {{der|en|it|tariffa}}, from {{der|en|ota|تعرفه|tr=ta'rife}}, from {{der|en|fa-cls|تَعْرِفَه}}, from {{der|en|ar|تَعْرِفَة||tariff, rate}}, from the root {{ar-root|ع ر ف|nocat=1}}.
{{root|en|ar|ع ر ف}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtæɹɪf/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-tariff.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtæɹəf/|a=GA|/ˈtɛɹəf/<a:Mary-marry-merry>}}<ref>{{R:Merriam-Webster Online}}</ref>
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtæɹəf/|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{wp}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[system]] of [[government]]-[[impose]]d [[duties]] [[levied]] on [[import]]ed or [[export]]ed [[goods]]; a [[list]] of such duties, or the duties themselves.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2004|author=Michael B Gross|title=The war against Catholicism
|passage=For the sake of this support, the party advocated for agricultural '''tariffs''', for antimargarine laws, and for restrictions on meat importation.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2012|author=Bert van Selm|title=The Economics of Soviet Breakup
|passage=Possibly Wallonians bought goods in Flanders that they could have obtained cheaper in Holland if it were not for the '''tariff'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Katie Lobosco|title=Trump’s trade war looms over soybean farmers 4 years later|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2022/05/08/politics/soybean-farmers-china-tariff-trump|date=2022-05-08|passage=It’s been nearly four years since China put '''tariffs''' on American-grown soybeans during a tit-for-tat trade war with then-President Donald Trump – and they remain in place despite the change in administrations.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=David Goldman and Clare Duffy|title=Trump threatens 25% tariff on Apple and says Samsung and other tech companies could be next|magazine=w:CNN|url=https://www.cnn.com/2025/05/23/economy/trump-threatens-tariff-apple|date=2025-05-23|passage=Speaking to press in the Oval Office on Friday after signing executive orders, Trump said the '''tariff''' would apply to any phone maker selling devices in the US.}}
# A [[schedule]] of [[rate]]s, [[fee]]s or [[price]]s.
#* '''1906''', Department of Commerce and Labor. Bureau of Manufactures, ''Monthly Consular and Trade Reports'' (number 313, page 75)
#*: There is a '''tariff''' in every carriage, and most of them also have taxometers.
# {{lb|en|British}} A [[sentence]] determined according to a [[scale]] of [[standard]] [[penalties]] for certain [[categories]] of [[crime]].

